Package: udr
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, rsync, openssh-client
Description: rsync over UDT for long, fast links
 udr runs rsync with its data channel on UDT, a reliable transport on UDP,
 instead of the ssh connection. ssh logs in and starts udr on the far side;
 the transfer then runs over one UDP port, picked from a range on the host
 that receives. On a link with a long round trip and some loss, UDT's
 congestion control can keep the link fuller than TCP does.
 .
 udr must be installed on both hosts. Its -n option encrypts the data
 channel with a cipher that carries no integrity check, and it is not a
 substitute for a tunnel; see udr(1).
